# Tuneflix Black & White Admin Starter

A starter full-stack admin app using Node.js + Express + PostgreSQL + vanilla HTML/CSS/JS.

## Included
- Black/white responsive admin UI
- Admin sign-in with hashed passwords and JWT
- Dashboard counters from PostgreSQL
- User/artist applications and approve/reject
- Label creation/listing
- Release submission/listing and approve/reject
- Audio/cover upload endpoint
- Wallet transaction ledger
- Support ticket listing/submission endpoint
- Notifications creation/listing
- Health endpoint at `/api/health`

## Run locally
1. Install Node.js 20+ and PostgreSQL.
2. Copy `.env.example` to `.env`.
3. Fill `DATABASE_URL`, `JWT_SECRET`, `ADMIN_EMAIL`, and a strong `ADMIN_PASSWORD`.
   Do not use the example password.
4. Run `npm install` then `npm start`.
5. Open `http://localhost:10000`.

The first admin is created automatically on first start only if `ADMIN_EMAIL` and `ADMIN_PASSWORD` are set and the password is not the example placeholder.

## Deploy on Render
1. Create a managed PostgreSQL database in Render.
2. Create a Web Service connected to your GitHub repository.
3. Build command: `npm install`
4. Start command: `npm start`
5. Add environment variables from `.env.example`. Use the Render PostgreSQL internal connection string where possible; set `PGSSL=true` if your database connection requires SSL.
6. Add a persistent disk mounted at `/opt/render/project/src/uploads` if keeping uploaded audio/cover files on the web service. Better for production: use object storage (S3/R2/Supabase Storage) and store permanent object URLs in PostgreSQL.
7. Set `ADMIN_EMAIL`, a strong `ADMIN_PASSWORD`, and a long random `JWT_SECRET`.

## Important before replacing your live Tuneflix
This is a standalone starter, not a patch to your current application. It does not know your existing framework, database schema, user sessions, upload provider, or API routes. **Do not overwrite your current GitHub repository or production service with it until your existing code is backed up and the schema/routes are reconciled.**

## Production work still required
- Integrate with your existing database and user accounts before migration.
- Move uploads to durable object storage; local Render filesystem is ephemeral unless a persistent disk is attached.
- Add audit logs, password reset, email verification, CSRF strategy if cookie auth is adopted, stronger per-role permissions, payment gateway integration, royalty statement imports, streaming-platform reporting integrations, and automated tests.
- Payment entries here are an admin ledger only. No bank transfer, UPI payout, or payment gateway is executed.
- Analytics graph/stream totals require real DSP reports or imported stream data; this starter does not invent streams.
- Restrict CORS to your production domain and rotate all secrets before production.

## API quick reference
- `POST /api/auth/login`
- `GET /api/auth/me`
- `GET /api/health`
- `GET /api/dashboard` (admin)
- `POST /api/users/register`
- `GET /api/users` (admin)
- `PATCH /api/users/:id/status` (admin)
- `GET|POST /api/labels` (admin)
- `GET|POST /api/releases` (admin list; authenticated submission)
- `PATCH /api/releases/:id/status` (admin)
- `GET|POST /api/wallet/transactions` (admin)
- `GET|POST /api/support` (authenticated)
- `GET|POST /api/notifications` (admin)
